---
title: Contact
nav: contact
layout: base.njk
---
<section class="hero" style="min-height:280px;">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <h1>Contact <span class="accent">Us</span></h1>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:48px;">
    <div>
      <h2>Get In Touch</h2>
      <div class="content-placeholder">
        <strong>Content needed:</strong> I don't have your dad's real phone number, email, physical address, or business hours yet. Send me those (or a screenshot of the Contact page) and I'll replace this placeholder.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Send a Message</h2>
      <form class="contact-form">
        <label>Name<br><input type="text" name="name" required style="width:100%; padding:10px; margin-bottom:16px;"></label>
        <label>Email<br><input type="email" name="email" required style="width:100%; padding:10px; margin-bottom:16px;"></label>
        <label>Message<br><textarea name="message" rows="5" required style="width:100%; padding:10px; margin-bottom:16px;"></textarea></label>
        <button type="submit" class="btn">Send Message</button>
      </form>
      <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--color-gray-mid); margin-top:12px;">Note: this form isn't wired up to actually send emails yet — once we pick a hosting provider I'll connect it (e.g. Netlify Forms or Formspree) so submissions land in your dad's inbox.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
